  "id": "developmental-dysgraphia",
  "term": "developmental dysgraphia",
  "definition": "Developmental dysgraphia is a developmental difficulty with writing and spelling that is closely related to developmental dyslexia. The source indicates that affected children can show different underlying cognitive patterns, including problems in phonological processing as well as auditory or visual processing linked to spelling ability.",
